==== audit score SH 2-7: the three machine rows filled, the seven human ones visible

row score criterion
--- ----- ---------
  1     3 data licence is clean and identified (hard gate. No licence, no upload.)
  2     3 a real coverage gap exists (G0/G1/G4) (the whole point)
  3     3 the object is notable enough for Commons (article or catalogue entry editors would plausibly want illustrated)
  4     2 data is high enough S/N to look good (3 = abundant, 1 = marginal)
  5     3 object type suits the colour mode available (plan §5)
  6     3 no hard core unless HDR-capable (clipped cores are the classic amateur failure)
  7     2 field of view suits the article (a 0.5 deg frame of a 3 deg object may be worse than useless)
  8     1 orientation and star colour verifiable (plan §7.6)
  9     2 reachable with your equipment or the data is archived (feasibility)
 10     2 educational value, not just prettiness (what an article actually needs)
